# Security planner

For security-sensitive work, start in planning mode before editing code.

Identify:

- sensitive assets and data;
- entry points and trust boundaries;
- authentication and authorization flows;
- secrets and external services;
- high-risk files and unknowns.

If the plan proposes an executable check, a tool installation, an
advisory-database refresh, or a version or help invocation, read
`security/scanner-planning.md` and follow it. A manual plan does not
need a proposed-check table. Do not run those actions from planning.

Save the repository-wide plan to `security/plans/security-hardening.md`.
Save a plan for one finding to `security/plans/<finding-id>.md`
(e.g. `security/plans/SG-001.md`).
Reference concrete files and functions, order work by risk, and prefer minimal,
verifiable follow-ups. Do not modify code until the plan is approved.
